  <section id="who">
    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>PATV is a community website and set of chat bots built around live Camfrog video chat rooms. It is run by Houseplants LLC ("we", "us"). In these terms "the service" means the website at publicaccess.tv and its sub-sites, the Pepe bot in Camfrog rooms, our Discord and Twitch bots, and the APIs behind them.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="eligibility">
    <h2>2. Eligibility (18+)</h2>
    <p>The service is for adults. You must be <b>at least 18 years old</b> (or the age of majority where you live, if that's higher) to create an account or use the service. The Camfrog rooms, pads and feed can contain mature conversation and, where marked, adult content. If we learn an account belongs to someone under 18 we will close it.</p>
    <p>You can't use the service if we've previously banned you, or if the law where you are forbids it.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="accounts">
    <h2>3. Your account and its security</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Give accurate sign-up details and keep your email address current — it's how you get back into your account.</li>
      <li>You're responsible for what happens under your account. Keep your password private, use one you don't use anywhere else, and tell us at <a href="mailto:support@publicaccess.tv">support@publicaccess.tv</a> if you think someone else has access.</li>
      <li>One person, one main account. Extra accounts made to dodge a ban, farm bonuses, inflate votes or reports, or win PAT games against yourself aren't allowed. Bot accounts need our permission.</li>
      <li>Usernames that impersonate someone, a pad or PATV staff, or that are hateful or sexual, may be changed or removed.</li>
      <li>We may archive accounts that have been inactive for a long time; we tell you first in your inbox and on the site where we can.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="linked">
    <h2>4. Camfrog, Discord and Twitch</h2>
    <p>You can link a Camfrog name (by typing <code>!verify</code> to Pepe), a Discord account or a Twitch account. Linking lets the service treat them as you — for PAT, games, posts and moderation. Those services are run by other companies under their own terms and privacy policies; we aren't responsible for them, and you must follow their rules too. Using PATV doesn't change anything about your relationship with them.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="content">
    <h2>5. Your content</h2>
    <h3>You own it</h3>
    <p>"Your content" is anything you post or send through the service: feed posts, comments, pictures, audio, video, links, profile details, chat and mic audio in Camfrog rooms the service mirrors, and so on. You keep whatever rights you have in it.</p>
    <h3>The licence you give us</h3>
    <p>So we can run the service, you give us a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to host, store, copy, re-encode (for example resizing pictures or converting video), display, transcribe, translate, distribute and show your content on and through the service, and to let other users see and share it as the service allows (for example a post's share link). This licence is only for operating, promoting and improving the service. It ends when you delete the content or your account, except where (a) others have already re-shared it inside the service, (b) we need to keep it for moderation, safety, legal or backup reasons for a limited time, or (c) the law requires us to keep it.</p>
    <h3>You're responsible for it</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>You confirm you have the rights and permissions needed to post it — including the consent of anyone recognisable in a picture, video or recording.</li>
      <li>You're responsible for your content and the consequences of posting it. We don't endorse what users post and don't check everything before it appears.</li>
      <li>Public Camfrog room activity (public chat, who is in the room, who's on the mic, and what is said on the mic, which is automatically transcribed) can be shown on the website to members. Anything you say publicly in a room Pepe sits in may appear there. Private messages are never shown.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="rules">
    <h2>6. What isn't allowed</h2>
    <p>Don't post, send, stream or link to anything, or behave in any way, that:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>is illegal</b> where you are or where we are, or promotes or helps someone commit a crime;</li>
      <li><b>sexualises minors in any way</b> — child sexual abuse material (CSAM) and any sexual content involving someone under 18, real or simulated. <b>Zero tolerance:</b> it is removed, the account is banned permanently, and we report it to the relevant authorities (the National Center for Missing &amp; Exploited Children (NCMEC) via its CyberTipline, as required by 18 U.S.C. § 2258A, and law enforcement where appropriate) with the information we hold;</li>
      <li><b>is intimate imagery of someone shared without their consent</b> (including "revenge porn", hidden-camera content and sexual deepfakes of real people), or threatens to share it;</li>
      <li><b>harasses or bullies</b> someone — targeted insults, pile-ons, unwanted sexual comments, stalking, or continuing after being asked to stop;</li>
      <li><b>doxxes</b> someone — posts or threatens to post private information such as a home address, phone number, workplace, real name (when not public), or identity documents;</li>
      <li><b>threatens or incites violence</b>, or glorifies violent extremism or self-harm;</li>
      <li><b>attacks people for who they are</b> — race, ethnicity, national origin, religion, caste, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability or serious illness;</li>
      <li><b>is spam</b> — unsolicited ads, scams, phishing, chain posts, repeated junk, fake engagement, or vote / report manipulation;</li>
      <li><b>impersonates</b> another person, a pad, a brand or PATV staff, or misleads people about who you are in a harmful way;</li>
      <li><b>infringes someone's rights</b> — copyright, trademark, privacy or publicity rights — for example uploading music, film or streams you don't have permission to share;</li>
      <li><b>contains malware</b> or tries to break, overload, scrape at scale, probe or get around the security, rate limits or moderation of the service, or to access accounts or data that aren't yours;</li>
      <li><b>is adult content that isn't marked NSFW</b> (see below);</li>
      <li>uses PAT, games, markets or wagers to cheat, launder value, or exploit a bug — report bugs instead.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For the friendly, everyday version — including how much room there is for swearing, dark humour, roasting and hot takes — see <a href="/guidelines">Padiquette</a>, our site-wide guidelines. Pads can add rules of their own on top; if Padiquette and these terms ever disagree, these terms win.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="nsfw">
    <h2>7. Adult (NSFW) content</h2>
    <p>Legal adult content is allowed on the feed <b>only when it's marked NSFW</b> (the 🔞 box when you post) and only where the pad it's posted to allows it. Marked posts are blurred and hidden from visitors who aren't signed in. Admins and pad owners may mark, unmark or remove posts. Everyone shown in adult content must be an adult who consented to it being made and shared. The only exception is an AI-generated picture or video made under the <a href="/guidelines#ai">AI rules in Padiquette</a>: it may show a real, identifiable adult in a suggestive but non-sexual way (for example, a public figure in swimwear), and it must be marked NSFW. It must never show a real, identifiable person nude or in a sexual or sexualised way, never involve anyone who is or looks under 18, and the rest of these terms (harassment, impersonation, privacy and publicity rights) still apply. Never post adult content in a profile picture, username or pad listing.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="pepe">
    <h2>8. Pepe and automated features</h2>
    <p>Pepe is an automated bot. His replies, voices, DJ picks, summaries, transcripts and pictures are generated by software, including AI models, and can be wrong, odd or offensive — don't rely on them for anything important, and they aren't statements by us. Mic transcripts are automatic and may mis-hear people. Pepe's room snaps and clips (<code>!snap</code>, <code>!clip</code>) capture what's publicly visible in a room at that moment; people can opt out of being shown by name with <code>!incognito</code> or <code>!bridge hide</code>. AI pictures and videos made with Pepe (<code>!imagine</code>, <code>!video</code>, the feed's Generate) follow the <a href="/guidelines#ai">AI rules in Padiquette</a>: suggestive content is allowed and marked NSFW; explicit nudity, anything sexual involving minors, and sexual depictions of real people are not.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="pat">
    <h2>9. PAT and virtual items</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>PAT is a virtual points system for fun inside PATV. It has no cash value.</b> PAT and anything bought with it (cosmetics, items, stakes, market shares, lottery tickets and so on) are not money, currency, securities, deposits or property, and can't be redeemed, exchanged or cashed out for money, goods or anything of value outside the service, by us or anyone else.</li>
      <li>You get a limited, personal, revocable licence to use PAT and virtual items within the service. You don't own them. Selling, buying or trading PAT, items or accounts for real money or anything outside PATV is not allowed.</li>
      <li>PAT games, markets, wagers, staking and vaults are entertainment. Balances, odds, prices, rewards and rules can change, and we may adjust, reverse, reset or remove PAT or items — for example to fix a bug or an error, undo cheating or abuse, keep the economy balanced, or when an account is archived or closed. No refunds or compensation are owed for PAT or virtual items.</li>
      <li>PAT may be shown with numbers, charts or words borrowed from finance ("staking", "vaults", "markets", "returns"). These describe game mechanics only and are not financial products or advice.</li>
      <li><b>Looking ahead:</b> we may explore other ways for PAT to work in the future. Nothing on the service is a promise or an offer about that. If anything ever changes the nature of PAT, it will come with new terms that you'd be asked to accept separately; until then this section applies in full.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="rooms">
    <h2>10. Pad owners</h2>
    <p>Some pads have owners who can moderate their pad's feed: approve, hide, pin, mark NSFW, remove posts from their pad, lock comments and ban people from posting there. Pad owners must follow these terms, use those tools in good faith, and must not use them to harass people or to hide content that should be reported to us. Owners don't see the private information described in our Privacy Policy. Site admins can review or reverse any pad-level action.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="moderation">
    <h2>11. Moderation and appeals</h2>
    <p>We, our admins and pad owners may (but don't have to) review, label, hide, remove or restrict content and accounts, at any time, when we believe it breaks these terms, puts someone at risk, or exposes the service to legal trouble. Depending on how serious it is we may warn you, remove content, limit posting, reporting or PAT features, ban you from a pad or the whole feed, or close your account. Automated limits (rate limits, new-account limits, auto-hiding after several reports) apply too.</p>
    <p><b>Appeals:</b> if you think we got it wrong, email <a href="mailto:appeals@publicaccess.tv">appeals@publicaccess.tv</a> from the address on your account within 30 days, with your username, what was actioned and why you think it should be reconsidered. A different admin from the one who acted will look at it where possible. We'll tell you the outcome. Decisions about CSAM and other illegal content are not reversed.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="reporting">
    <h2>12. Reporting and copyright notices</h2>
    <h3>Reporting content or people</h3>
    <p>Use <b>Report</b> in the ⋯ menu on any post or comment, or <b>Report user</b> on a profile. Pick the closest reason and add a note if it helps. Reports of sexual content involving a minor hide the content immediately and go straight to the site admins. Reports about posts in a pad also go to that pad's owner, except legal and safety categories (child safety, non-consensual imagery, copyright), which only site admins see. You'll get an inbox update when we've acted on your report. Making reports in bad faith can pause your ability to report.</p>
    <p>For urgent safety issues or anything you can't report on the site, email <a href="mailto:abuse@publicaccess.tv">abuse@publicaccess.tv</a>. If someone is in immediate danger, contact your local emergency services first.</p>
    <h3>Copyright (DMCA) notices</h3>
    <p>We respect copyright and respond to valid notices. If you believe content on PATV infringes your copyright, send a notice to our designated agent:</p>
    <p>Copyright agent: Designated Copyright Agent, Houseplants LLC<br>Postal address: 228 Park Ave S, New York, NY 10003<br>Email: <a href="mailto:copyright@publicaccess.tv">copyright@publicaccess.tv</a></p>
    <p>Your notice should include: (1) your physical or electronic signature; (2) the work you say is infringed; (3) the link(s) to the material on PATV; (4) your name, address, phone number and email; (5) a statement that you have a good-faith belief the use isn't authorised by the owner, its agent or the law; and (6) a statement, under penalty of perjury, that the notice is accurate and that you're the owner or authorised to act for them. Misrepresenting that material is infringing can make you liable for damages.</p>
    <p>If your content was removed after a notice and you believe that was a mistake, you can send a counter-notice to the same address with: your signature; the material removed and where it appeared; a statement under penalty of perjury that you believe in good faith it was removed by mistake or misidentification; your name, address and phone number; and your consent to the jurisdiction of the Federal District Court for the judicial district in which you reside, or, if you reside outside the United States, any judicial district in which Houseplants LLC may be found (17 U.S.C. § 512(g)(3)(D)) and to accept service from the person who sent the notice. We close the accounts of repeat infringers in appropriate circumstances.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="termination">
    <h2>13. Ending your use of PATV</h2>
    <p>You can stop using the service at any time, and you can ask us to delete your account by emailing <a href="mailto:support@publicaccess.tv">support@publicaccess.tv</a> from the address on it. We may suspend or end your access, or close your account, if you break these terms, if we're required to by law, if your account has been inactive for a long time, or if we stop offering the service. When an account ends, its PAT and virtual items end with it. Sections that by their nature should survive (for example 5, 9, 14–18) continue to apply.</p>
  </section>

